#: ../../source/docs/using-linux-trace-toolkit-ng-lttng-to-trace-ardupilot-in-realtime.rst:7
#: ecf8c5ba60604474a8b3935ddda89caf
msgid "This article explains how to use `LTTng <https://lttng.org>`__ for creating runtime traces for ArduPilot running on Linux boards (only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-linux-trace-toolkit-ng-lttng-to-trace-ardupilot-in-realtime.rst:11
#: 6ba7c06cc51d4326b10334ee1f231ba7
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-linux-trace-toolkit-ng-lttng-to-trace-ardupilot-in-realtime.rst:13
#: 4590ef29cc12470f91be6d49e187ac73
msgid "Tracing is a technique used to record the real-time behaviour of a software in memory and analyze the execution of the code off-line. It can be very useful to understand the interaction between threads, processes, the duration of certain events and the sequencing of some operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-linux-trace-toolkit-ng-lttng-to-trace-ardupilot-in-realtime.rst:19
#: 0d8c5f06c85244339af8938d2c672fdb
msgid "*LTTng* is a Linux tool that can be used to trace either a userspace application, or the Linux kernel itself. It produces trace files that can be analyzed later, mostly off-board. Lttng's implementation in ArduPilot uses userspace tracing but you can at the same time monitor what's going on inside the kernel, provided the kernel has tracepoints enabled (in its config)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-linux-trace-toolkit-ng-lttng-to-trace-ardupilot-in-realtime.rst:26
#: 606f34a04fe44e9488d826280515227a
msgid "*LTTng* has been integrated using the `Perf_Lttng <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_Linux/Perf_Lttng.cpp>`__ class, which handles 3 operations: ``Begin``, ``End``, ``Count``. You add tracing to your code by calling the performance utility methods in `Perf.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_Linux/Perf.cpp>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-linux-trace-toolkit-ng-lttng-to-trace-ardupilot-in-realtime.rst:33
